{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344834-flight-telekinesis-and-teleportation-using-the-\u0441orrespondence-sphere","id":1344834,"title":"Flight, telekinesis and teleportation using the \u0421orrespondence Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T21:51:52-07:00","id":1344834,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Flight, telekinesis and teleportation using the \u0421orrespondence Sphere","content":"Good afternoon. Need help with Spheres.<br /> My hero is a verbena witch. I want her to fly on a broomstick, like Harry Potter, and be able to make \u201cflying ointment\u201d to give other people the opportunity to fly. What spheres are needed for this? The text in the book can be understood in many ways. There were also questions on telekinesis and teleportation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>M</b><b>20, </b><b>sphere</b> <b>Forces</b><b>, </b><b>level</b> <b>3:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Transmute Minor Forces/ Telekinetics/ The Dragon\u2019s Touch<br /> Now the mage can alter and invoke the energies she could only touch before. By adding Prime 2, she may conjure winds, fire, electricity, gravitational wells, and so forth. Combining this Rank with Life or Matter, she can transform people into electricity (Life 5/ Forces 3); change water into air (Forces 3/Matter 3<b>), or attach elemental force to material forms \u2013 making them fly</b>, pinning them to the ground, and having other, similar effects <b>(generally with Life or Matter 3).</b> And by adding an ephemeral Sphere to this Rank, she might erode or enhance energies (Entropy 3); manifest thoughts into energies (Mind 3); transmute spirit-stuff into physical energies (Spirit 3); or set triggers for energy fluctuations at some later interval (Time 4). At this Rank, the scale of effect grows larger, now encompassing several dozen yards or a handful of characters. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage revised, sphere Forces, level 3:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Transmute Minor Forces<br /> Finally able to grasp and twist the Patterns of forces, a skilled mage can convert forces into other types, shift their intensity radically or even create force from nothing (and banish it to oblivion as well). Although he is still able to affect only individual small Patterns of force, the mage can cause the elements to dance at his whim. He can impart motion into an object, make a fire that burns cold or cause shadows to explode into bursts of light. <b>Mages can use this power to fly</b>, hurl lightning, pulse out electronics and perform similarly dramatic feats. The mage cannot create force from nothing without the use of Quintessence, but he can turn minor forces to his own advantage.<br /> <b>In conjunction with Pattern magic</b>, the mage can convert a force into an object or even a creature, or disperse a material<br /> into raw energy. <b>He can easily weave telekinetic controls around a creature or object</b>, and he can cause his attacks to pass through objects or creatures harmlessly on their way to the target. Similarly, with the ephemeral Spheres he can transmute a pure idea into a construct of force, lay waste to a distant location or set up a special attack that waits until an appropriate time or event comes to pass. </div> </div> </div>It turns out that according to the Revised rules, I only need Forces 3 to fly myself, and Forces 3 + Life 3 to move other people by telekinesis.<br /> It is incomprehensible, to give other people the opportunity to fly (to the scene, for example), I only need Forces 3 or Forces 3 + Life 3?<br /> When moving the target with telekinesis, I have to make a roll at each movement, or once I get success I can move the victim the whole scene, how do I want?<br /> <br /> According to the rules of M20, I need Forces 3 + Life 3 in all cases: both to fly myself, and to give someone the ability to fly, and to move someone by telekinesis. Right? This makes flying ability very expensive on dots ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>M</b><b>20, </b><b>sphere</b> <b>correspondence</b><b>, </b><b>basic</b> <b>description</b><br /> By manipulating the ties between places, objects, and people, the Correspondence Sphere allows a mage to sidestep distances, sense things that would normally be out of range, <b>pull objects out of thin air, levitate or fly</b>, or connect an Effect to some other place or character. Some mages proclaim this Sphere is proof that distance is an illusion, whereas others view it as the Art of pulling strings between different places and people. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>M20, sphere correspondence, level 3:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Pierce Space/ Open or Close Gates/ Co-locality Perceptions<br /> Now the mage can tear holes in space, large enough for her<br /> to step through. These minor gates are small and temporary, but they allow that character to step from one place to another, so long as she\u2019s alone and lightly encumbered. (Teleporting large items, or while carrying heavy loads, demands Correspondence 4.) Scoping out the new location is a good idea, of course. A close, familiar destination requires fewer successes than a distant, unfamiliar one.<br /> Using the Co-locality Perceptions Effect, the mage can also perceive several places at once. Those locations all appear as ghosts overlapping each other, as if they\u2019d been layered on top of the closest location.<br /> Also<b>, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter</b>, the mage can move things around from a distance<b>, levitating, manipulating</b> or teleporting <b>them without physical contact</b>. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage revised, sphere correspondence, basic description (abbreviated)</b><br /> Space, interrelationships and sympathetic links all become clear through the study of Correspondence.<br /> By bending space or bypassing it entirely, a mage can travel rapidly, <b>fly or teleport</b> from place to place. Divining locations allows the mage to see far-away places or direct magic over distances. With a link between a person and an object, Effects may be targeted through connecting rituals\u2026<br /> \u2026 Despite its capacity to bend space and distance, Correspondence functions only on whole Patterns unless combined<br /> with the various Pattern Spheres. That is, it\u2019s impossible to just teleport away someone\u2019s heart with Correspondence alone. In essence, Correspondence does not affect Patterns directly; such manipulations must be done with other magic. Correspondence simply lets those Patterns be affected, whole and complete, in changes of space or distance. If the mage wants to use Pattern Spheres to affect something with Correspondence, she\u2019s limited by the Correspondence level (if it\u2019s lower than the Pattern Sphere). Thus, a <b>mage can teleport something with just Correspondence</b>, but if she wants to <b>change its Pattern at a distance</b>, her skill with Correspondence is as important as her skill <b>with the other Sphere</b>. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage revised, sphere correspondence, level 3:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Pierce Space/ Seal Gate/ Co-locality Perception<br /> Tearing the very fabric of space itself, the mage can open a brief gateway to other places and step through. While the mage could only cast her senses out to distant locations previously, she can now actually travel via teleportation. The mage needs only sense the destination \u2014 or even haphazardly cast out to a random place, although doing so is extremely dangerous \u2014 then perform an appropriate Effect to change her Pattern\u2019s location.<br /> Drawing together connections in various Patterns \u2014 or severing them \u2014 is also possible, and it causes the Patterns affected to build a stronger or weaker bond that can be exploited later through Correspondence.<br /> By strengthening the bonds of space instead of warping them, a mage can seal gateways and block the passage of Correspondence Effects. The mage can actually bar an area from passage, be it mundane or through Correspondence. Such an Effect prevents transportation in an area, and it can be cast over Patterns other than the mage herself.<br /> Finally, moderate comprehension of Correspondence allows a mage to split his perceptions over several locations at once. Although the mage can open a door to only a single place, or manipulate individual Patterns without major effort, she can use her scrying to view multiple places simultaneously. The mage could experience the show in any form appropriate to her paradigm. She might see a set of ghostly superimposed images around her as she spies on multiple locations, or perhaps she has a series of small simultaneous images for different places.<br /> <b>With Pattern Spheres</b>, the mage can use Correspondence to <b>teleport Patterns</b> or <b>move objects from a distance</b>. The mage reaches out and bypasses space to touch the object from range. Searching through multiple locations at once lets the mage perform very acute investigations, especially when using other Spheres to look for specific results. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage revised, sphere correspondence effects:</b><br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Apportation </b>\u2014 Although the rudiments of Correspondence are insufficient to actually teleport safely over long<br /> distances, a mage can affect some small Patterns. A quick Effect <b>causes an object or creature to transport to or from the mage</b>. <b>The mage must also use the appropriate Pattern Sphere, typically Life or Matter</b>. Apportation can\u2019t affect any Pattern more complex than the mage\u2019s Correspondence knowledge. That is, even a Master of Life or Matter can transport only very simple Patterns with this limited understanding of Correspondence (plants and very simple animals for Life, basic homogenous substances for Matter).<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Seven-League Stride </b>\u2014 Legend has it that the Order of Hermes made magical boots that would take the wearer exactly seven leagues with each stride. Though such boots are an artifact of the past, this Effect mirrors their capabilities. A competent mage can step from place to place nearly instantaneously. Depending on the exact sort of magic used, the mage might seem to blur past in an instant, or just vanish and reappear somewhere else. Regardless, the mage effectively teleports to any place he desires, although near and better-known locations are easier to reach, of course.<br /> <b>Just as a mage can teleport himself through judicious use of Correspondence, objects or creatures can be moved with the right Effect</b>. Simple Apportation can affect only simple Patterns, but as the mage\u2019s Correspondence knowledge improves, she can affect similarly more complex Patterns<b>. Simple living things or composite objects can be moved</b> with variations on the Seven-League Stride. Adepts and Masters of Correspondence can even use their greater rituals to bring along other people or to transport large or unusual substances.<br /> Combined with Correspondence Sensing, the mage can travel to just about any place that can be scried \u2014 which is a good thing if the mage doesn\u2019t want to land in a hostile environment by accident. With Sense Connection, the mage could detect a scrying adversary, trace that connection and then teleport to the spy. </div> </div> </div>It turns out that according to the Revised rules, I only need Correspondence 3 to teleport myself.<br /> To teleport another person, are Correspondence 3 enough, or are Correspondence 3 + Life 3 needed? The description of the sphere says \u201cmage can teleport something with just Correspondence\u201d, another conclusion is drawn from the description of the effect.<br /> To move someone in space, you need Correspondence 3 + Life 3? Should I roll at each move, or once I get success I can move the victim the whole scene, as I want?<br /> To levitate on my own, I only need Correspondence 3 or do I need Correspondence 3 + Life 3? Can levitation be interpreted as flight? Or do I need a roll for every move? Is the flight Correspondence 3 (Pierce Space) or Connections 5 (Mutate Localities)? What is the difference between levitation and flight in terms of mechanics?<br /> Can I use Correspondence 3 + Life 3 to endow another with the ability to levitate (on scene, for example)?<br /> <br /> According to the rules of M20, I only need Correspondence 3 to teleport myself, passing through the short-term gates.<br /> I need Connections 3 + Life 3 to teleport or move someone without physical contact. And if I touch a person I can only teleport him with only Correspondence 3? Technically, do I also open short-term gates?<br /> <br /> Please sorry for bad English <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25740-platinumangel","user":"platinumangel","date":". 10-31-2019, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25740-platinumangel","name":"platinumangel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T23:33:42-07:00","id":1344846,"title":"","content":"You don't need Life 3 to target someone. You MIGHT need it to say target someone's heart or something if you wanted to teleport it out of their chest but if you just want them to fly its.. Forces.<br /> <br /> Correspondence lets you target things out of your line of sight it doesn't do what you think it does. You CoULD sort of fly by &quot;teleport... drop.. teleport.. drop..&quot; but.... its probably just easier to teleport.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T00:35:48-07:00","id":1344853,"title":"","content":"The only time life would be needed is if you wanted to do what M20 likes to talk about with 'locking it onto the pattern'. Otherwise you're just controlling the area around someone, not necessarily making it so they fly around on their own.<br /> <br /> The difference is real minor and I dislike it to begin with. Mostly because it winds up just being a Life 2 (simple) life 3 (human ) tax or a matter 2 tax on literally everything.<br /> <br /> Don't you need Correspondence 4, and corr 4 alone, to teleport other people? I know Correspondence 3 is self. The text on Corr 3 doesn't help alleviate confusion on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T00:37:05-07:00","id":1344855,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm aware the M20 rules were reviewed to make the spheres more balanced in their use so where they contradict the revised rules I would err on the side of the newer rules. There have been a lot of 'creative interpretations' of the spheres over the years (i.e. players breaking the rules and getting away with it) and how they are interpreted largely depends on your storyteller and local group of players.<br /> <br /> Additionally the system is designed to allow the same effect to be attained via different spheres under different paradigms - look at Chi Healing (I think?) to see an example of an expensive way to heal a character.<br /> <br /> That said requiring two spheres at 3 dots or one sphere at 4 dots to create a significant effect like flying/teleporting is not exactly what most players would describe as 'very expensive'. It's at the limit of what a starting character can do but not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:03:59-07:00","id":1345050,"title":"","content":"I don't think M20 requires you to have Forces and Life in order to be able to fly, though it is a bit oddly worded.<br /> <br /> Making yourself fly should be 3 Forces. Note you would definitely need more than 1 success to do this (if nothing else to extend the duration of the spell).<br /> Making others fly I'm not so sure about. Here's where you have to make a judgement call.<br /> <br /> If you controlled their flying I think just having forces would be okay.<br /> <br /> If you gave someone wings and used forces to lighten them, I'd definitely would say you would need life 3 or maybe even 4 and forces 3. But an ointment? Not sure how that works. Maybe a single dot of prime to shift control of the spell to them? Honestly never thought about shifting the control of a long duration spell to someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","name":"CoriolisEffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:24:28-07:00","id":1345059,"title":"","content":"Why would flying be forces 3. Forces 2 is controlling forces. Forces 3 is turning one force into another. Why would you use forces 3 to control gravity/wind to move yourself into the air? Even the default magick chart lists flying as Forces 2. You grab gravity/your force of choice, and push it somewhere else to move.<br /> Converting forces is unnecessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Fun fact it also says you can fly with matter 2 but I have no fucking idea why/where they get that)<br /> <br /> It also lists Correspondence 3/Life 2 as a way of flying so I have no fucking idea what the hell is going on. Unless the idea is you are locking a constant 'teleport' pattern onto someone so they are just teleporting microinches forward at rapid speeds to stimulate flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:18:40-07:00","id":1345394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344834-flight-telekinesis-and-teleportation-using-the-\u0441orrespondence-sphere?p=1345059#post1345059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would flying be forces 3. Forces 2 is controlling forces. Forces 3 is turning one force into another. Why would you use forces 3 to control gravity/wind to move yourself into the air? Even the default magick chart lists flying as Forces 2. You grab gravity/your force of choice, and push it somewhere else to move.<br /> Converting forces is unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more so that Forces: 3 would allow you to better establish/maintain flight via transforming ambient (F)orces around you (gravity, the kinetic force from local wind currents, (sun)light, et al) into a more directed kinetic (F)orce so as to provide ongoing flight. (Forces:2 can simulate levitation, kinetic adherence, gliding and similar more readily, but the energies it controls/directs will diminish as-used; Forces:3 -- especially if fortified with Prime:2 -- allows the magic to better &quot;self-fuel&quot; and maintain itself more readily.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344834-flight-telekinesis-and-teleportation-using-the-\u0441orrespondence-sphere?p=1345059#post1345059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also lists Correspondence 3/Life 2 as a way of flying so I have no fucking idea what the hell is going on. Unless the idea is you are locking a constant 'teleport' pattern onto someone so they are just teleporting microinches forward at rapid speeds to stimulate flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence, when combined with the Pattern Spheres, does a lot more than &quot;just&quot; teleport -- you can create sustainable spatial warping around/through the targeted (P)attern and cause it to move through space. You can levitate/cause-to-move something with Correspondence:3 and either Life:2 or Matter:2 (as they act to lock the effect onto the target and then slide them along through space). This has been a concept across the editions of the game since the 90s; Correspondence, as stressed by the writers and a number of people around these parts, is more than just the &quot;teleporting&quot; Sphere... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (For a better metaphysical perspective, it works the same way that a Ban does except spatially &quot;reversed&quot; in a certain context -- instead of being used to bar things from interacting with the target (which can also still be included in the effect with some more successes), it &quot;draws along&quot; the target across space. In Star Trek, it's similar to how many applications of warp drive and applied subspace fields work; in fact, in older Trek reference manuals, with incredibly precise even by their tech-standard's calculations, a warp field can be inverted so as to &quot;punch a hole&quot; in space and allow instantaneous travel... though at great risk, hence why Star Fleet and others banned the technique. That inverting, however, is how Correspondence:3/4 manifests teleportation in Mage.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T00:30:15-08:00","id":1345723,"title":"","content":"Big thanks for your answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25740-platinumangel","name":"platinumangel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:10:40-08:00","id":1345734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344834-flight-telekinesis-and-teleportation-using-the-\u0441orrespondence-sphere?p=1344855#post1344855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm aware the M20 rules were reviewed to make the spheres more balanced in their use so where they contradict the revised rules I would err on the side of the newer rules. There have been a lot of 'creative interpretations' of the spheres over the years (i.e. players breaking the rules and getting away with it) and how they are interpreted largely depends on your storyteller and local group of players.<br /> <br /> Additionally the system is designed to allow the same effect to be attained via different spheres under different paradigms - look at Chi Healing (I think?) to see an example of an expensive way to heal a character.<br /> <br /> That said requiring two spheres at 3 dots or one sphere at 4 dots to create a significant effect like flying/teleporting is not exactly what most players would describe as 'very expensive'. It's at the limit of what a starting character can do but not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly. What they did was find every excuse in the book to make magic useless unless you have all your spheres at 4-5.<br /> <br /> It's very clear that the writers very much preferred the other game lines to Mage. If the page long screed on why the Vampire Lawn Chair meme wasn't clear enough, the bit about needing to use Correspondence magic to call a cab or private Helicopter that you actually own/have the means to access mundanely was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:58:00-08:00","id":1346095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344834-flight-telekinesis-and-teleportation-using-the-\u0441orrespondence-sphere?p=1345734#post1345734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not particularly. What they did was find every excuse in the book to make magic useless unless you have all your spheres at 4-5.<br /> <br /> It's very clear that the writers very much preferred the other game lines to Mage. If the page long screed on why the Vampire Lawn Chair meme wasn't clear enough, the bit about needing to use Correspondence magic to call a cab or private Helicopter that you actually own/have the means to access mundanely was.</div> </div> </div> </div>This forum needs a &quot;wat&quot; reaction button. Where is this hyperbole coming from? I think you're putting things into a way more extreme light - and amusingly partially in the opposite direction - than what M20 gave us, IMO.<br /> <br /> First of, M20 explicitely states that Correspondence does <i>*not*</i> coincidentally call a cab or helicopter you own. I'm not even sure how that'd make sense, unless you use 1st Edition result-based rules.<br /> <br /> Second, There is one big change between the base levels of the spheres that I've seen in the M20 corebook, and that's in <i>M20, you need Life 3 to heal others - instead of Life 4 in Revised</i>. There might have been something about Prime, but I don't remember, and couldn't spot it from a quick lookover.<br /> But if you claim that M20 ( aside of the controversial Nightfolk Countermagick rules and the cherrypicking-required nature of HDYDT, there is no argument there by anyone I think ) puts the big breaks on mages...uh. Where do I even begin?<br /> <br /> <i>Most</i> effects in M20 pretty much require the identical spheres and levels as Revised. Be it Flying, teleporting, enhancing your abilities or attacks with supernatural senses, conjuring things, transforming things, Really, if you pick the rank-and-file typical Mage stuff, nothing changed in the requirements. Healing others, as above, even got easier - starting characters can do it.<br /> <br /> If we look at other changes, any notions of &quot;Mages got nerfed in M20&quot; become even more strange to even consider:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) <b>Arete rolls</b>:<br /> <i>M20</i> -&gt; Default rule is that total Arete successes count towards all aspects of an effect. This includes targets. Only Damage or Duration need split successes if both are used at once.<br /> <i>Revised</i> -&gt; all the aspects had to be split between succeses, requiring a lot more and causing Mages to need extended rolls and Rituals way more.<br /> 2) <b>Paradox</b> for successful vulgar effects (others follow a similiar lessened pattern):<br /> <i>M20</i> -&gt; 1<br /> <i>Revised</i> -&gt; (highest sphere used)<br /> 3) <b>Backlashes</b>:<br /> <i>M20</i> -&gt; Start at total accumulated Paradox of around 5.<br /> <i>Revised</i> -&gt; Always instant punishment. You better have a Sanctum, or else.<br /> 4) <b>Instruments</b>:<br /> <i>Revised</i> -&gt; Start surpassing them at 5 for mystics. Technomancers and Technocrats? At 10.<br /> <i>M20</i>: -&gt; Start surpassing them at 3 for mystics, 5 for Technomancers. Never for Technocrats, but who seriously cares given that it was Arete 10 before.<br /> 5) <b>Conjuring patterns</b><br /> <i>Revised</i> -&gt; Conjuring forces requires Quintessence points. Conjuration of other patterns was never quite clear.<br /> <i>M20</i> -&gt; Devs explicitely stated that no Quintessence points are needed - even for Forces, if those only last for a round.<br /> <br /> <br /> That list above becomes <i>*seriously*</i> noticable if you've played M20 games for a while and go back to a Revised game. I've recently done so, and I immediately felt way more limited from several sides compared to M20.<br /> <br /> Your mileage clearly varies, hard - but I honestly do not quite get why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-05-2019, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T15:16:21-08:00","id":1346297,"title":"","content":"HDYDT or base M20 actually spends a fourth of the page basically laughing at the idea of using Correspondence 3 to teleport then saying &quot;I used a cab&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes through an elaborate as hell explanation of teleporting a cab to yourself, or creating one out of thing air.<br /> <br /> And then suggests using Entropy 2 (Or 3) and just hoping you get enough successes for a cab to just happen to go by.<br /> <br /> It's great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}